om/u/26803198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter","html_url":"https://github.com/LordDeatHunter","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T17:39:37Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T17:42:00Z","body":"I tried several things, but was unable to replicate your scenario.\r\nWhat I assume happened is, you had point index 10 pinned in the project the previous time you tested (importing the original zip, it does indeed show up as selected in the array editor, but not visually) and now since this visual point contains 2 physical points, with 1 of them being de-selected, it visually shows it as such. In fact, point 10 was still selected even in the 2nd zip you sent (in the array editor, not visually, since there's a deselected overlapping point):\r\n<img width=\"418\" height=\"153\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/83b59420-0765-459c-98d5-bedbce26ae1d\" />\r\n<img width=\"1304\" height=\"887\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b86675fb-9276-4852-8dd3-7d01ac827457\" />\r\n(the point in question, index 10, with 142 as the overlap point, coordinate axis for convenience)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIn a realistic scenario, users can click the \"old points\" to deselect them, and click again to select all the overlapping ones.\r\nFurthermore, (as long as you can't replicate this from clicking or other such actions) I don't quite see this as a bug. The visual clicking adding all the overlapping points is a QoL improvement, but it shouldn't be forced on the users. If a user wants to select 1 specific physical point manually without all the overlapping ones, they should be able to do so (via array editor or in code).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit: I think I got your point after writing the entire comment - at this point, my solution no longer matches with the title of the PR. I can re-add the highlight as long as _any_ point in the overlap is selected.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353197735/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353955460","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110493#issuecomment-3353955460","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110493","id":3353955460,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H6UyE","user":{"login":"LordDeatHunter","id":26803198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2ODAzMTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26803198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter","html_url":"https://github.com/LordDeatHunter","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LordDeatHunter/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.g